Bring the USB-C port up as a sink

`tcpm` makes a dual-role port source-first when its connector is
`self-powered`, which is the wrong way round for a phone that only ever
charges from a cable: the port then never runs BC1.2 or PD on the sink
side, the charger reports no USB type at all, `qcom_smb5` keeps retrying
APSD, and the input current stays at the 500 mA default.

Declaring the port a sink fixes the role at probe time.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-xiaomi-alioth.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-xiaomi-alioth.dts
@@ -1,9 +1,9 @@
 	connector {
 		compatible = "usb-c-connector";
 
-		power-role = "dual";
+		power-role = "sink";
 		data-role = "dual";
 		try-power-role = "sink";
-		self-powered;
+		/* a phone only ever charges from a cable */
 
 		op-sink-microwatt = <33000000>;
